{
  "_note": "LEVEL 2. Level 1 is waves.json; levels.json says which is which. Same thirteen waves and the same shape as level 1 \u2014 the same spawn groups in the same order, at the same intervals and delays \u2014 with the demons substituted tier for tier: Underling for Scrapper, Middle Manager for Buckethead, The Devil for The Politician. Bruiser stays where he was, so the early waves are not wall-to-wall demons.",
  "_health": "Total enemy health is 29945 against level 1's 25274, which is +18.5% across the run. That comes from the demons being tougher one-for-one (52/185/6200 against 40/140/4600) minus five Middle Managers trimmed out of waves 6, 9, 11 and 12 to keep it inside the 15-20% band, plus one Bruiser added to each of the first three waves so level 2 opens a step above level 1 rather than identical to it. The stats themselves are enemies.json's and are not touched here.",
  "_spacing": "SPACING IS LEVEL 1'S, UNCHANGED, and that is a measurement rather than an oversight. Level 2's lane is 1916.7px against level 1's 1976.9px \u2014 3.0% shorter, which is about a third of a second of walking at Bruiser speed. Copying the intervals reproduces level 1's pacing to well inside what a player can feel; scaling them by 0.97 would be arithmetic dressed up as tuning. If the lane changes materially later, this is the note to revisit.",
  "_economy": "Shared with level 1: rules.json is not per-level. This run pays 0.141 peanuts per point of enemy health against level 1's 0.148.",
